description:
Change under review: add "duplicate document" to the documents API. Only the changed region of the file is shown: lines 58-67 are new, the handlers above them are unchanged, and the rest of the file is unchanged.

`src/routes/documents.ts` (changed, lines 40-67):
```ts
40 app.patch("/documents/:id", requireSession, async (req) => {
41   const doc = await documents.get(req.params.id);
42   await assertCan(req.session.user, "edit", doc.folderId);
43   return Response.json(await documents.update(doc.id, await req.json()));
44 });
45
46 app.post("/folders/:folderId/documents", requireSession, async (req) => {
47   await assertCan(req.session.user, "edit", req.params.folderId);
48   const { title, body } = await req.json();
49   return Response.json(await documents.create(req.params.folderId, { title, body }));
50 });
51
52 app.delete("/documents/:id", requireSession, async (req) => {
53   const doc = await documents.get(req.params.id);
54   await assertCan(req.session.user, "edit", doc.folderId);
55   return Response.json(await documents.remove(doc.id));
56 });
57
58 app.post("/documents/:id/duplicate", requireSession, async (req) => {
59   const source = await documents.get(req.params.id);
60   await assertCan(req.session.user, "view", source.folderId);
61   const { targetFolderId } = await req.json();
62   const copy = await documents.create(targetFolderId ?? source.folderId, {
63     title: `${source.title} (copy)`,
64     body: source.body,
65   });
66   return Response.json(copy);
67 });
```

`assertCan(user, action, folderId)` throws a 403 error unless the user holds that permission on the folder. Folders belong to different teams, and view and edit permissions are granted separately; many users can view a folder they cannot edit. Existing middleware enforces CSRF protection on every state-changing route: the session cookie is `SameSite=Strict`, and a request without a valid `X-CSRF-Token` header is rejected.
